WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.057
Parsing and formatting move in opposite directions.

00:00:03.057 --> 00:00:07.542
Parsing starts with text and creates a typed date or timestamp.

00:00:07.542 --> 00:00:13.387
That typed value can be sorted, compared, grouped, and used in arithmetic.

00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:19.417
Formatting starts with a typed temporal value and creates text for human presentation.

00:00:19.417 --> 00:00:23.107
For analytics, parse early and format late.

00:00:23.107 --> 00:00:30.332
Parsing converts text into a typed value; formatting converts a typed value into presentation text.

00:00:30.332 --> 00:00:36.922
Perform analytical work on typed dates and timestamps, then format near the presentation layer.

00:00:36.922 --> 00:00:43.372
If parsing can fail, validate the incoming pattern first instead of letting one malformed value stop an entire

00:00:43.372 --> 00:00:44.640
load.
